From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: do not log -EEXIST on flow
 refresh

Only the SNAT direction of a connection is programmed into the PPE, so
the reply direction keeps crossing the software flowtable path. Every
such packet runs flow_offload_refresh(), which -- at most once a second
per flow -- re-offers the flow with FLOW_CLS_REPLACE. The flow is already
in our table, so ppe_offload_flow_replace() returns -EEXIST, exactly as
mtk_ppe_offload does for the same re-offer, and the flowtable ignores it.

The failure log did not distinguish this expected case, so a router with
a handful of live connections printed "replace failed at exists: -17"
continuously (some 220 lines, plus ratelimit suppression, over 20 minutes
of two iperf3 flows on the bench). Skip the log for -EEXIST; genuine
programming failures still print.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c
@@ -743,7 +743,15 @@ deref_pub_ip:
 unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->lock);
 
-	if (stage)
+	/* -EEXIST is not a failure: flow_offload_refresh() re-offers a
+	 * flow that is already in hardware once a second for as long as
+	 * its packets keep crossing the software path -- which, with only
+	 * the SNAT direction accelerated (see the file comment), is the
+	 * reply direction of every accepted connection. mtk_ppe_offload
+	 * returns the same -EEXIST for this; only a genuine programming
+	 * failure is worth a line.
+	 */
+	if (stage && ret != -EEXIST)
 		pr_info_ratelimited("ppe_offload: replace failed at %s: %d\n", stage, ret);
 
 	return ret;
